        "original_id": "9a63bf63-230f-593c-b9c3-218785ce2be8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Zymer Bytyqi, Martin Ødegaard\n- Organizations: Viking, Sandnes Ulf, Red Bull Salzburg, SC Heerenveen, Real Madrid, Norway national team\n- Roles: winger, attacking midfielder\n- Topics: Norwegian football, player records, loans\n\nFacts:\n- Zymer Bytyqi was born on 11 September 1996 and is a Norwegian footballer.\n- Martin Ødegaard was born on 17 December 1998 and is a Norwegian professional footballer.\n- Zymer Bytyqi made his first-team debut in 2012 and became the youngest player ever to play in the Norwegian top league at that time.\n- Martin Ødegaard later broke Zymer Bytyqi’s record as the youngest player to play in the Norwegian top league.\n- Zymer Bytyqi plays as a winger for Viking.\n- Zymer Bytyqi previously played for Sandnes Ulf and Red Bull Salzburg.\n- Martin Ødegaard plays as an attacking midfielder for SC Heerenveen on loan from Real Madrid.\n- Martin Ødegaard also plays for the Norway national team.",
